            <ArticleTitle>[Acute abdominal pain due to a ventriculo-peritoneal shunt metastasis of an intracranial germ cell tumor].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>141-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Extracranial metastases of pineal germinomas are rare.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">The case of a metastasis of a primary intracranial germ cell tumor via a temporary-ventriculo-peritoneal shunt as a cause of acute abdominal pain is reported. The germ cell tumor markers were useful in establishing the diagnosis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">With an appropriate clinical history, intra-abdominal metastases via a temporary ventriculo-peritoneal shunt should be considered in the differential diagnosis of acute abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
